coder › Done on branch `work/parse-ini` (2 commits: `610f7f1 Implement parseIni in src/ini.ts`, `d7ed162 Add parseIni tests`).

What changed:
- `src/ini.ts`: implemented `parseIni`. Splits on `/\r?\n/`, trims each line, skips blanks and lines starting with `;`/`#`. `[name]` sets the current section (name trimmed, section object created lazily); keys before any header go under `''`. Key/value split on the first `=`, both sides trimmed; a value wrapped in double quotes (after trimming) has the quotes stripped with the inside kept verbatim. Later duplicate keys overwrite earlier ones. Anything else (bad section header, line without `=`, empty key) throws `SyntaxError('Invalid INI line <n>: <raw>')` with the 1-based line number.
- `src/ini.test.ts`: kept the existing test, added 7 tests covering: pre-section keys under `''`, whitespace trimming, comments/blank lines, quoted values preserving spaces and `;`, first-`=` split (`k=b=c`), key override, and `SyntaxError` naming the line number plus `instanceof SyntaxError`.

Checks (`bun test`, project's `test` script) — exact output:
```
